A||N||8||Hoostine||4 speed stuck in reverse||||1||
Z||000000||Hoostine||07-16-2001||10:38 PM||||so i put a battery in my new fiero today and i'm trying to get the thing to start.  it turns over a few times and i'm playing with it a bit and trying to figure out the shift pattern when i finally find reverse and put it in.  but, it won't come out.  the clutch doesn't work in the car (slave line is sitting on top of the car) and i think that's the problem.  i hope that's the problem.  i bought this car for the tranny, not the engine.  infact, all i want are the frame and tranny.  what's the problem?  the engine turns over btw, and with it in reverse, it'll move the car a bit.  i need to get that clutch line fixed so i can go driving a bit.<P>--Hoostine||||reg||1
Z||000001||Steve Normington||07-17-2001||12:38 AM||||With the engine not running, you should be able to shift out of reverse with or without the clutch. Have you looked at the shift cables to see if they are binding? If PO had been speed shifting, the shift cable could bind in the sleeve and prevent you from shifting.||||reg||1
Z||000002||StuGood||07-17-2001||06:21 PM||||Well, if something is putting torque onto the  wheels while it's in reverse (like, if the car's parked on a slope), and the clutch isn't releasing, it won't want to shift out of reverse.  'Cause of the pressure placed on the gear teeth - reverse is a sliding gear.<P>Kind of a dumb answer, you probably already knew this, but thought I'd mention it just in case.  Have you tried rocking the car (with the engine off, of course) while shifting out of reverse? ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Hoostine||07-18-2001||12:22 AM||||heh, nope, haven't tried rocking it...<BR>will tho, tomorrow.<P>haven't checked the cables either.  it'll move side to side, but not up and down.  the shifter came out of the reverse spot.  but the trans didn't.<P>--Hoostine||||reg||1
Z||000004||StuGood||07-18-2001||09:37 AM||||Okay - as long as I'm in the habit of pointing out stuff you probably already know and/or tried...<P>Since the shift lever moved but the trans. didn't get itself out of reverse, something slipped.  The preferable thing would be if a cable housing came loose from its bracket, or the nut on the end of the cable (not you  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> )<BR>is loose (so it slipped in the slot on the lever on top of the trans.).  OR (less likely but possible) the lever at the tranny came off - there's a big nut on the end f the shift shaft, which normally holds the lever on.<P>Might try rocking the car (by hand, with engine off) with the rear hood open, while you try to operate (rotate) the lever on top of the trans., to knock it out of reverse.<P>If the lever on the trans. rotates, but it doesn't come out of reverse- well, you don't want to know...           ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fiero_24||07-18-2001||10:24 AM||||Just a thought, but my 85 SE stuck in first gear.  Lets just say it was cheaper to swap the tranny out than to have it fixed.  I tried rocking, pulling, messing with the linkage, and no luck at all.<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||4
Z||000006||Hoostine||07-18-2001||05:04 PM||||i took off the shifter cables today, and the levers wouldn't move.  well, the side to side(at the shifter) one moved, but the other one wouldn't.  i'm going to wait till i get the clutch line put back on and see if i can get the trans out of reverse, and if it won't come out, i guess i'll have to just get a getrag 5-spd(darn!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">).<P>i can't rock the car, one tire is flat and 4 are low and it doesn't like moving at all.  we had to drag it off of the car trailer with a truck.  it rolled, but didn't like it.  maybe the brakes are locked up.  one day i'll find a jack small enough to get under it so i can jack it up and take the wheels off and check ...<P>--Hoostine||||reg||1
